Just a quick rundown on the terminology:

- A section is the smallest unit of BPFK work, done by a shepherd
- A checkpoint is a collection of sections, which are deemed to belong together because of interconnectedness. A checkpoint is completed (approved) when all of its sections are approved.

As I understand it, you want Ted to start working on Intensifiers right away. Is this correct?

